      "Diary Note": "**Regular Audio Setting**\n2025-09-12, Friday, 21:12-22:19\n\nI hung out today and thought about how important audio is in VR but also how tricky it is to set up. The world is super popular, but the loud background music made a soft microphone test totally unreliable. I really couldn't tell if my voice was okay in the main room. So, I asked a friend, Ivy, for some help. I walked with her to a much quieter private booth in the back. I asked her how my voice sounded, and she said she could hear me clearly at a normal speaking volume. That was a relief! But she also noticed a sharp burst of distortion whenever I laughed or spoke louder. Ah, this feedback is exactly what I needed. It prompted me to make one small gain reduction in my mic settings, just lowering the slider a tiny bit. It was fixed quickly, and we happily went back to chatting without worrying about hurting anyone's ears.",
